#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0047 expect=noViolation domain=ADAE
#note "PLAN-library-template-label-resolution R2-1 (owner 2026-10-04), on OUR metadata store: a run that declares only ADaMIG 1.1 resolves ADAE against the D10-inferred OCCDS 1.0, whose base Req names STUDYID, USUBJID, --SEQ, --TERM, CMTRT and AESER. A '--' name resolves to the dataset's source domain - its occurrence variables AESEQ / AETERM name AE - so --SEQ / --TERM are demanded as AESEQ / AETERM; CMTRT carries the CM prefix (the store's description opens with CM.CMTRT) and is not demanded of an AE dataset, AESER (AE.AESER) is. Every demanded name is present -> silent. Before R2-1 this reported [--SEQ, --TERM, CMTRT] missing (the P5 stop, both pilots)."
#library-ref standard=adamig version=1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AEDECOD type=Char label="Dictionary-Derived Term"
col AESER type=Char label="Serious Event"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1 | HEADACHE | HEADACHE | N
---
